<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|<tuple|generic>>

<\body>
  Smile \<#1F600\> rocket \<#1F680\> heart \<#2764\>\<#FE0F\> flag
  \<#1F1EE\>\<#1F1F9\> family \<#1F468\>\<#200D\>\<#1F469\>\<#200D\>\<#1F467\> thumb
  \<#1F44D\>\<#1F3FD\> keycap #\<#FE0F\>\<#20E3\> end.

  Every emoji above is drawn in layers of colored glyphs, which stand for
  no character: it must extract as its characters, a sequence (the flag,
  the family, the skin tone, the keycap) whole, in a reader which takes
  the text from the ActualText of the spans as much as in one which takes
  it from the character map of the font.
</body>

<initial|<\collection>
  <associate|font|roman>
</collection>>
